WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:09.320
Boredom is one of the most consuming and disheartening
conditions that a human can be stricken with.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:14.960
In the true sense of the term, boredom is
the monotonous and lifeless experience of

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.070
life itself.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:23.109
To be frequently bored is to be out of sync
and disconnected from life.

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:26.900
It is not a natural or useful experience.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:32.880
It is a result of one’s over attachment
to daily routine.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.870
Routine is a part of life.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:41.700
We love the comfort and consistency that routine
gives us and we fear the uncertainty that

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.629
comes with any deviation from it.

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:53.550
Our gravitation towards daily routine is likely
a reflection of our necessity for internal

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:54.649
routine.

00:00:54.649 --> 00:01:02.379
We require consistent internal functions in
order to maintain physiological health.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:10.690
For the purpose of survival, our heartbeat,
breath, blood flow, digestive processes, regulatory

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:16.510
brain functions, and so on must all adhere
to routine.

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:23.970
In order to ensure this, though, our brain
often casts the net of routine over our entire

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.170
life.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:32.290
When we accept this paradigm of routine, though,
we ignore the fact that our daily life does

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:36.970
not have to always match our physiological
one.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:45.090
A life founded entirely on routine does not
fulfill the more conscious component of human

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:46.860
existence.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:53.640
When we live too heavily with routine, we
may be alive on the inside, but we are dead

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.960
on the outside.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:02.770
Understanding the different forms of routine
helps one begin to properly strain them from

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:07.790
one another and apply them appropriately to
life.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:14.829
Activities that support internal physiological
functions should be kept in routine.

00:02:14.829 --> 00:02:21.680
Keeping on a relative schedule for things
like eating, sleeping, meditating, exercising,

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:28.420
and so on, allow your body to fulfill the
patterns necessary for a physically healthy

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:30.400
life.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:38.200
Activities that support the conscious enjoyment
of life should be removed from routine.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:46.900
Things like work habits, travels, social engagements,
recreations and other things alike.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:53.849
These elements of life should be far less
regimented and more spontaneous.

00:02:53.849 --> 00:03:00.409
The only way to stimulate the psychological
experience of life is with spontaneity and

00:03:00.409 --> 00:03:01.719
wonder.

00:03:01.719 --> 00:03:09.000
It is important that we maintain spontaneity
in life, for spontaneity keeps life fresh,

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.950
while routine dries it out.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:17.719
We should fear the things that temporally
take us out of boredom, but further attach

00:03:17.719 --> 00:03:20.099
us to routine.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:23.980
Things like checking social media every other
minute.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.849
Or watching too much TV.

00:03:26.849 --> 00:03:29.069
Or excessive drinking.

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:31.090
Or heavy drug use.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:33.260
Or binge eating.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:39.900
Or whatever else one can fill their life up
with to distract themselves from disillusion

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.790
and a lack of excitement.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:49.340
These kinds of things distract us from our
boredom but do not eliminate it.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:56.139
They in fact fuel the loop of boredom and
restrict us to temporary solvents.

00:03:56.139 --> 00:04:02.239
We pile as much temporary relief into our
lives and eventually find ourselves buried

00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:06.109
beneath it all, covered in boredom.

00:04:06.109 --> 00:04:12.440
In order to avoid this, begin conditioning
yourself out of routines.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:18.470
Start small by reducing meaningless habit-forming
activities.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:23.720
Try new things, new people, new places, and
so on.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:32.030
Push your comfort-zone and let opportunities
carry you in and out of routine, without fear.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:39.040
Feel the freshness and wonder that comes from
progression and new experience.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:48.570
Feel the life.

